---
import LearningLayout from '../../../layouts/LearningLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/Icon.astro';
import { NETWORK_NODES, NETWORK_EDGES, SHOPS, UPGRADE_COST, HOURS_COST, MODEL_VERSION } from '../../../lib/scenario';
const point=(id:number)=>({x:60+NETWORK_NODES[id].x*110,y:55+NETWORK_NODES[id].y*100});
---
<LearningLayout title="Explore a food-access scenario" section="scenario" intro="Choose shops, change an illustrative offer and compare who can reach it. This is a synthetic neighbourhood model, not a forecast for any real area.">
  <div class="scenario-boundary"><span class="status-pill">Model output · not a study finding</span><p>The model tests walking time, basket affordability and opening hours. It does not simulate purchasing, nutrition or health, and it does not apply the trial risk ratio to these different outcomes.</p></div>
  <noscript><p class="notice">JavaScript is required to run the scenario. The model assumptions and evidence links remain readable below.</p></noscript>
  <div class="scenario-workspace" data-scenario>
    <aside class="scenario-controls"><form id="scenario-form"><fieldset disabled id="scenario-controls"><legend>Intervention choices</legend><div class="scenario-field"><label for="scenario-budget">Setup budget <output id="budget-output" for="scenario-budget">£6,000</output></label><input type="range" id="scenario-budget" name="budget" min="0" max="20000" step="500" value="6000"/><p class="control-help">Illustrative setup cost: £2,000 per shop, plus £500 for later opening. Ongoing retailer or subsidy costs are not modelled.</p></div><div class="scenario-field"><label for="offer-price">Basket price at selected shops <output id="offer-output" for="offer-price">£14</output></label><input type="range" id="offer-price" name="offerPrice" min="8" max="24" step="1" value="14"/><p class="control-help">This replaces the current price, so setting it higher can reduce access.</p></div><label class="checkbox-label"><input type="checkbox" id="extend-hours" name="extendHours"/> Offer later opening at selected shops</label><fieldset class="shop-choices"><legend>Choose shops to change</legend>{SHOPS.map((shop,i)=><label class="shop-choice"><input type="checkbox" name="shops" value={shop.id}/><span class="shop-letter">{String.fromCharCode(65+i)}</span><span><strong>{shop.name}</strong><small>£{shop.price} basket · {shop.lateOpening?'late opening':'daytime only'}</small></span></label>)}</fieldset><div class="allocation-cost"><span>Setup allocation</span><strong id="allocation-cost">£0 / £6,000</strong></div><button type="button" class="button button-primary" id="scenario-preset">Try a two-shop example <Icon size={16}/></button><button type="button" class="reset-link" id="scenario-reset">Reset to baseline <span aria-hidden="true">↺</span></button><details class="assumption-controls"><summary>Population assumptions</summary><div class="scenario-field"><label for="travel-assumption">Available shopping time</label><select id="travel-assumption" name="travelAssumption"><option value="0.8">20% less time</option><option value="1" selected>Central assumption</option><option value="1.2">20% more time</option></select><p class="control-help">Changes the assumption for both baseline and alternative, not an intervention benefit.</p></div><div class="scenario-field"><label for="population-seed">Synthetic population seed</label><input id="population-seed" name="seed" type="number" min="0" max="999999" step="1" value="42"/><p class="control-help">The same seed reproduces the same fictional households. No local demographic data are used.</p></div></details></fieldset></form></aside>
    <div class="scenario-main"><p id="scenario-status" class="scenario-live" role="status" aria-live="polite">Preparing the scenario model…</p><p id="scenario-error" class="scenario-error" role="alert" hidden></p><div class="neighbourhood-panel"><div class="chart-panel-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Invented neighbourhood · 100 m between junctions</p><h2>Six shops, 200 households</h2></div><div class="map-mode"><label for="map-view">Map view</label><select id="map-view"><option value="scenario">Alternative</option><option value="baseline">Baseline</option></select></div></div><svg id="neighbourhood-map" viewBox="0 0 560 520" role="img" aria-labelledby="neighbourhood-title neighbourhood-description"><title id="neighbourhood-title">Fictional food-access neighbourhood</title><desc id="neighbourhood-description">A grid of streets, six shops and 200 synthetic households. Select shops using the labelled controls. Green circles have modelled access and outlined circles do not. Exact overall and group counts are in the results table; an inspected household's route is described below.</desc><rect x="12" y="12" width="536" height="496" rx="14" class="map-ground"/>{NETWORK_EDGES.map(([a,b])=><line x1={point(a).x} y1={point(a).y} x2={point(b).x} y2={point(b).y} class="street-outline"/>)}{NETWORK_EDGES.map(([a,b])=><line x1={point(a).x} y1={point(a).y} x2={point(b).x} y2={point(b).y} class="street-line"/>)}<g id="household-dots" aria-hidden="true"></g><polyline id="inspected-route" points="" class="inspected-route" aria-hidden="true"/><circle id="route-traveller" r="6" class="route-traveller" visibility="hidden" aria-hidden="true"/>{SHOPS.map((shop,i)=><g data-map-shop={shop.id} aria-hidden="true"><rect x={point(shop.nodeId).x-19} y={point(shop.nodeId).y-17} width="38" height="34" rx="7" class="map-shop"/><text x={point(shop.nodeId).x} y={point(shop.nodeId).y+5} text-anchor="middle" class="map-shop-letter">{String.fromCharCode(65+i)}</text></g>)}</svg><div class="neighbourhood-legend"><span><i class="household-key access"></i> Modelled access</span><span><i class="household-key no-access"></i> No modelled access</span><span><i class="shop-key"></i> Selected shop</span></div><div class="household-inspector"><label for="household-select">Inspect a synthetic household</label><div><select id="household-select" disabled><option>Waiting for model</option></select><button type="button" id="animate-route" class="small-button" aria-pressed="false" disabled>Animate route</button></div><p id="household-detail">Household constraints and the selected route will appear here.</p></div></div>
      <div id="scenario-results" hidden><div class="scenario-metrics"><div><span class="metric-label">Baseline access</span><strong id="baseline-access">—</strong><span>of 200 synthetic households</span></div><div><span class="metric-label">Alternative access</span><strong id="alternative-access">—</strong><span>of the same 200 households</span></div><div><span class="metric-label">Change in access</span><strong id="access-change">—</strong><span>households meeting all criteria</span></div></div><p class="results-definition">Access means at least one affordable shop with compatible opening hours, reachable within the household’s time allowance, including the return walk and 10 minutes shopping.</p><div class="data-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scenario access by profile table"><table class="learning-table"><caption>Access by synthetic household profile — 50 households in each group</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Profile</th><th scope="col">Baseline</th><th scope="col">Alternative</th><th scope="col">Change</th></tr></thead><tbody id="group-results"></tbody></table></div><p class="travel-summary" id="travel-summary"></p><details class="methods-disclosure" open><summary>Variation and sensitivity</summary><div><p id="population-variation"></p><p class="small">The 10th–90th percentile ranges describe variation across 40 synthetic population draws. They are not confidence intervals for a real population and do not include uncertainty about the model’s structure or empirical evidence.</p><div class="data-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scenario sensitivity checks table"><table class="learning-table"><caption>Paired sensitivity checks: change the available-time assumption for both baseline and alternative</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Time assumption</th><th scope="col">Baseline access</th><th scope="col">Alternative access</th></tr></thead><tbody id="sensitivity-results"></tbody></table></div></div></details><div class="scenario-savebar"><button type="button" class="small-button" id="save-scenario">Save current result as A</button><button type="button" class="small-button" id="download-scenario">Download scenario JSON <Icon name="download" size={16}/></button></div><section id="saved-comparison" class="saved-comparison" hidden><h3>Saved A and current result</h3><p id="saved-comparison-text"></p><p class="small">Saved A is held only in this tab. Download its JSON before leaving if you want to keep it.</p></section></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="learning-section" id="assumptions"><p class="eyebrow">Evidence and assumption ledger</p><h2>What drives the model?</h2><div class="data-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scenario evidence and assumptions table"><table class="learning-table assumption-table"><caption>Model {MODEL_VERSION} — every numerical input below is an illustrative assumption</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Input or mechanism</th><th scope="col">Basis</th><th scope="col">Interpretation and limit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Street network and shops</th><td>Invented 5 × 5 grid; 100 m links; six shops.</td><td>No real streets or shop data. Paths follow the grid; barriers and crossing delays are absent.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Household profiles</th><td>200 synthetic households; 50 per profile; seeded variation in time, budget, speed and opening-hour needs.</td><td>Illustrates unequal constraints, not the demographic composition of either area. No race- or ethnicity-based behaviours.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Affordability and time</th><td>Selected basket price must fit the household’s budget; round-trip walking time plus 10 shopping minutes must fit its time allowance.</td><td>These are model rules, not estimated behavioural relationships. The time sensitivity panel varies an assumption, not a measured effect.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Shop choice</th><td>Nearest affordable shop with compatible hours; deterministic tie-break.</td><td>Does not represent preferences, cultural acceptability, stock, queues, household interaction or changing behaviour.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Intervention costs</th><td>£{UPGRADE_COST.toLocaleString('en-GB')} setup per selected shop; £{HOURS_COST} additional setup for later opening.</td><td>Fictional budget units. Recurring retailer, staffing and subsidy costs are not estimated.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Trial purchasing estimate</th><td><a href="/learning/food-access/effects/">Six synthetic household-offer trials</a>.</td><td>Not a model input. A purchasing risk ratio does not estimate route access or the effect of geographically redistributing offers.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Qualitative context</th><td><a href="/learning/food-access/context/">Invented affordability, time, familiarity and trust findings</a>.</td><td>Motivates questions to discuss. No numerical multipliers are inferred from these narratives.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
  <div class="learning-notice"><Icon name="info"/><div><strong>A spatial scenario, not a calibrated agent-based forecast.</strong><p>Households have different constraints, but do not interact or adapt in this model. The synthetic exercise shows how assumptions change access. A commissioned module would need its own agreed purpose, evidence review, applicability assessment and validation appropriate to its intended use.</p></div></div>
  <script>import '../../../scripts/scenario-ui';</script>
</LearningLayout>
